00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  they arrived from many parts of the  capital manila hopeful and defiant  more than 700 000 supporters showed up  at ayala avenue  for decades it's been a place for  hosting large gatherings that often lead  to turning points in this nation's  history  as the leader of the opposition vice  president leni robredo started her  campaign  with meager resources  [Applause]  but her unique messaging based on what  she calls radical love quickly changed  the electoral landscape which for  decades had been about big money and  patronage politics  her grassroots campaign has galvanized  support from nearly all sectors of  society particularly young people they  are here young people they are putting  everything on the line for this campaign  they are sacrificing their time just so  they would see a better future under  president leni robredo  young people here tell us this is more  than just a regular campaign their  participation they say is an act of  defiance after years of president  rodrigo duterte's restrictive policies  and also a major pushback against the  possible return of the marcuses to the  presidency  it has been a tough fight from the start  between two very different candidates  robredo is a widow and a human rights  lawyer while her political rival  bongbong marcus jr is the son of the  late president ferdinand marcos was  ousted in a popular revolution in 1986  the marcus name has long been synonymous  with decadence and abuse of power  but bongbong has been leading opinion  polls here for months though many  experts say they may no longer reflect  the realities on the ground because from  house to house campaigns to flash mobs  to so-called volunteer truth armies  fighting this information  many say robredo's campaign has become a  people's movement  [Music]  and on monday filipinos will decide  whether all this will have been enough  for robredo to win an election that is  seen as the most consequential in recent  history alindogan al jazeera 